      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SIR GOLDALOT (3) saves all his best racing for his home track here, and he won his penultimate start here in this grade with 59kg, and then was narrowly beaten as the favourite last week, finishing third. He steps up to a middle distance for the first time this season, and with 60.5kg to carry back in this rightful class, he is still the one to beat. HEADLINE LEGEND (5) had been to the fore at the picnic meetings last month, and brought that form to Gatton 8 days ago when leading all the way to score a comfortable win over 2000m by a length. He jumps up 3.5kg, but will still take some catching. FLIRTING WITH FIRE (7) won her maiden on protest here last week, but did deserve her victory. Now that the penny has dropped, she can go on with it. MARAVICH (2) looked to peak on his run late when fresh up here 3 weeks ago over 1640m, and the extra 260m is the ideal next step. If he does not need this run as well, then he will be a top 3 hope again. ",
